      "message": "This patch is part of a broader security hardening effort that includes:\n - 45+ fixes across 25 files in frameworks/base, system/core, lineage-sdk, hardware, and recovery\n - Memory safety fixes: unchecked malloc/calloc null dereferences (12 HAL modules), unbounded caches, use-after-free patterns\n - Concurrency fixes: unsafe signal handlers (llkd, snapuserd), singleton volatilty, async-signal-safety violations\n - Crypto hardening: BTI/PAC on armv8-a, expanded CFI coverage, integer overflow sanitizers, branch protection\n - SELinux hardening: backuptool domain restricted to eng-only, recovery enforcing on userdebug\n - Supply chain: world-writable debug files fixed (0777→0600), directory permissions hardened\n These tests validate the security-critical fixes in this chain — without them, the listener cleanup paths (TwilightTracker memory leak, ProfileTriggerHelper ContentObserver leak, ChargingControlController receiver leak) have no automated verification.\n\n The same methodology was applied to ParrotOS custom kernel hardening, where AI-assisted analysis detected and mitigated multiple security vulnerabilities including CopyFail variants, with validation from security researchers. The LineageOS patches follow the same rigorous approach: automated audit → manual review → fix → test → Gerrit review.\n\n If you need search the mitigations ParrotOS custom kernel you have visit: https://github.com/MethodWhite/kernel-security-patches\n\n Assisted-by: OpenCode:deepseek-v4-pro\n---",
